This image redistributes model weights obtained from Hugging Face.

  Model:     MoritzLaurer/deberta-v3-base-zeroshot-v2.0
  Revision:  8e7e5af5983a0ddb1a5b45a38b129ab69e2258e8
  Files:     the onnx/ directory at that revision, placed at the top level
  Base:      microsoft/deberta-v3-base
  License:   MIT (as declared on the model card at that revision)
  Author:    Moritz Laurer, as named on the model card
  Used by:   llm-guard 0.3.16, BanTopics scanner (MODEL_DEBERTA_BASE_V2)
  Mirrored:  2026-10-24, from https://huggingface.co at the revision above

File integrity. For model.onnx and spm.model the sha256 was read from the Hugging
Face API for that revision (the LFS object id) and independently computed from the
downloaded files, and they agree. The other five files are plain git blobs: their
git object ids from the API agree with the downloaded bytes, and the sha256 below
was computed from those bytes. The image build pins every file to these hashes.

  added_tokens.json        sha256 dc046d04c9b0ada7ae6f1dc89c465801799acdf0c9a6aab8c15a1b2d5ca4e91f
  config.json              sha256 a68162c0b02cd39759732b33d26ee2868cb64701b0b9255fee4f55fd9d5609f4
  model.onnx               sha256 d46fa6c1addc598abd34af8651120291f51417ddfce45b9d5f70bc32d3efa81c
  special_tokens_map.json  sha256 b2f1b2f15f29a6b6d9d6ea4eca1675d2c231a71477f151d48f79cc83a625ba21
  spm.model                sha256 c679fbf93643d19aab7ee10c0b99e460bdbc02fedf34b92b05af343b4af586fd
  tokenizer.json           sha256 bfead76cd475f67849a6710fdd16497f75732773e4d90e40d3b5bb5d3f031df9
  tokenizer_config.json    sha256 f5a1a74a632c0e9225e09a21ddf60c2e70ef5d3bfc1f261a24fd8ddab27254d2

No modification has been made to the weights.

The repository at that revision carries no LICENSE file. Its model card declares
`license: mit` in its metadata and says, under "License": "The foundation model was
published under the MIT license. The licenses of the training data vary depending
on the model, see above." The card also says that models without "-c" in the name,
this one included, "include data with non-commercial licenses" in their training
data, that "legal opinions diverge if this training data affects the license of the
trained model", and that "for users with strict legal requirements, the models with
'-c' in the title are recommended." The card names no copyright holder. The MIT
License terms follow.

